      "card_ids": ["C75","C76","C77","C78","C79","C80","C81","C82","C83","C84","C85","C86"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "No intravenous reference data are available for the query, so absolute F cannot be directly calculated.",
    "L6 hepatic clearance records are for other molecules; no direct query CLint or hepatocyte-stability measurement is available.",
    "L6 high-CLint records (C76,C80,C84) are less structurally transferable and/or from non-human assays, so their relevance to the query is uncertain.",
    "L3 Tmax records for moclobemide (C40/C41) confirm oral absorption but do not quantify F.",
    "First-pass metabolism and transporter-mediated disposition of the query remain experimentally uncharacterized."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because human-relevant L1/L2 bioavailability evidence for related molecules is consistently at or above 20%, L4/L5 support high absorption and low gut-wall efflux, and L6 low-clearance records for similar morpholine amides outweigh less transferable high-CLint records. Mixed L6 hepatic clearance evidence introduces first-pass uncertainty, so confidence is moderate; no affirmative evidence supports F < 20%."
}

